reference.api:
```
POST /v1/events/{id}/queue            → {queue_token, position_estimate}
GET  /v1/events/{id}/seats?section=   → {version, seats[{id, status, price}]}     (cached)
POST /v1/events/{id}/holds {seat_ids[], queue_token, idempotency_key}
                                      → 201 {hold_id, expires_at} | 409 {unavailable[]}
POST /v1/orders {hold_id, payment_token, idempotency_key} → 201 {order_id, tickets[]}
DELETE /v1/holds/{id}
```
- A hold needs a valid, unexpired queue token, so the seat service is protected from clients that skipped the waiting room.
- Holds are all-or-nothing: either every requested seat is held or none is.
